{"route":"/docs/5.3/layout/gutters/","version":"5.3","renderedVersion":"5.3","title":{"id":"content","type":"heading","en":"Gutters","level":1},"lead":{"id":"content--paragraph-1","type":"paragraph","en":"Gutters are the padding between your columns, used to responsively space and align content in the Bootstrap grid system."},"blocks":[{"id":"how-they-work","type":"heading","en":"How they work","level":2},{"id":"how-they-work--list-1","type":"list","tag":"ul","items":[{"tag":"li","body":[{"id":"how-they-work--item-1","type":"item","en":"<strong>Gutters are the gaps between column content, created by horizontal <code>padding</code>.</strong> We set <code>padding-right</code> and <code>padding-left</code> on each column, and use negative <code>margin</code> to offset that at the start and end of each row to align content."}]},{"tag":"li","body":[{"id":"how-they-work--item-2","type":"item","en":"<strong>Gutters start at <code>1.5rem</code> (<code>24px</code>) wide.</strong> This allows us to match our grid to the <a href=\"https://getbootstrap.com/docs/5.3/utilities/spacing\">padding and margin spacers</a> scale."}]},{"tag":"li","body":[{"id":"how-they-work--item-3","type":"item","en":"<strong>Gutters can be responsively adjusted.</strong> Use breakpoint-specific gutter classes to modify horizontal gutters, vertical gutters, and all gutters."}]}]},{"id":"horizontal-gutters","type":"heading","en":"Horizontal gutters","level":2},{"id":"horizontal-gutters--paragraph-1","type":"paragraph","en":"<code>.gx-*</code> classes can be used to control the horizontal gutter widths. The <code>.container</code> or <code>.container-fluid</code> parent may need to be adjusted if larger gutters are used too to avoid unwanted overflow, using a matching padding utility. For example, in the following example we’ve increased the padding with <code>.px-4</code>:"},{"id":"horizontal-gutters--example-1","type":"demo","key":"6c692653c0e7ca7651d3","height":147},{"id":"horizontal-gutters--code-1","type":"code","value":"<div class=\"container px-4 text-center\">\n  <div class=\"row gx-5\">\n    <div class=\"col\">\n      <div class=\"p-3\">Custom column padding</div>\n    </div>\n    <div class=\"col\">\n      <div class=\"p-3\">Custom column padding</div>\n    </div>\n  </div>\n</div>","language":"html"},{"id":"horizontal-gutters--paragraph-2","type":"paragraph","en":"An alternative solution is to add a wrapper around the <code>.row</code> with the <code>.overflow-hidden</code> class:"},{"id":"horizontal-gutters--example-2","type":"demo","key":"afc57d66e51f611fa6d3","height":147},{"id":"horizontal-gutters--code-2","type":"code","value":"<div class=\"container overflow-hidden text-center\">\n  <div class=\"row gx-5\">\n    <div class=\"col\">\n      <div class=\"p-3\">Custom column padding</div>\n    </div>\n    <div class=\"col\">\n      <div class=\"p-3\">Custom column padding</div>\n    </div>\n  </div>\n</div>","language":"html"},{"id":"vertical-gutters","type":"heading","en":"Vertical gutters","level":2},{"id":"vertical-gutters--paragraph-1","type":"paragraph","en":"<code>.gy-*</code> classes can be used to control the vertical gutter widths within a row when columns wrap to new lines. Like the horizontal gutters, the vertical gutters can cause some overflow below the <code>.row</code> at the end of a page. If this occurs, you add a wrapper around <code>.row</code> with the <code>.overflow-hidden</code> class:"},{"id":"vertical-gutters--example-1","type":"demo","key":"a316e9a220e5a690cc86","height":147},{"id":"vertical-gutters--code-1","type":"code","value":"<div class=\"container overflow-hidden text-center\">\n  <div class=\"row gy-5\">\n    <div class=\"col-6\">\n      <div class=\"p-3\">Custom column padding</div>\n    </div>\n    <div class=\"col-6\">\n      <div class=\"p-3\">Custom column padding</div>\n    </div>\n    <div class=\"col-6\">\n      <div class=\"p-3\">Custom column padding</div>\n    </div>\n    <div class=\"col-6\">\n      <div class=\"p-3\">Custom column padding</div>\n    </div>\n  </div>\n</div>","language":"html"},{"id":"horizontal--vertical-gutters","type":"heading","en":"Horizontal &amp; vertical gutters","level":2},{"id":"horizontal--vertical-gutters--paragraph-1","type":"paragraph","en":"Use <code>.g-*</code> classes to control the horizontal and vertical grid gutters. In the example below, we use a smaller gutter width, so there isn’t a need for the <code>.overflow-hidden</code> wrapper class."},{"id":"horizontal--vertical-gutters--example-1","type":"demo","key":"76dd58cc38bef2794b66","height":147},{"id":"horizontal--vertical-gutters--code-1","type":"code","value":"<div class=\"container text-center\">\n  <div class=\"row g-2\">\n    <div class=\"col-6\">\n      <div class=\"p-3\">Custom column padding</div>\n    </div>\n    <div class=\"col-6\">\n      <div class=\"p-3\">Custom column padding</div>\n    </div>\n    <div class=\"col-6\">\n      <div class=\"p-3\">Custom column padding</div>\n    </div>\n    <div class=\"col-6\">\n      <div class=\"p-3\">Custom column padding</div>\n    </div>\n  </div>\n</div>","language":"html"},{"id":"row-columns-gutters","type":"heading","en":"Row columns gutters","level":2},{"id":"row-columns-gutters--paragraph-1","type":"paragraph","en":"Gutter classes can also be added to <a href=\"https://getbootstrap.com/docs/5.3/layout/grid#row-columns\">row columns</a>. In the following example, we use responsive row columns and responsive gutter classes."},{"id":"row-columns-gutters--example-1","type":"demo","key":"60de1c5c3bd356449656","height":147},{"id":"row-columns-gutters--code-1","type":"code","value":"<div class=\"container text-center\">\n  <div class=\"row row-cols-2 row-cols-lg-5 g-2 g-lg-3\">\n    <div class=\"col\">\n      <div class=\"p-3\">Row column</div>\n    </div>\n    <div class=\"col\">\n      <div class=\"p-3\">Row column</div>\n    </div>\n    <div class=\"col\">\n      <div class=\"p-3\">Row column</div>\n    </div>\n    <div class=\"col\">\n      <div class=\"p-3\">Row column</div>\n    </div>\n    <div class=\"col\">\n      <div class=\"p-3\">Row column</div>\n    </div>\n    <div class=\"col\">\n      <div class=\"p-3\">Row column</div>\n    </div>\n    <div class=\"col\">\n      <div class=\"p-3\">Row column</div>\n    </div>\n    <div class=\"col\">\n      <div class=\"p-3\">Row column</div>\n    </div>\n    <div class=\"col\">\n      <div class=\"p-3\">Row column</div>\n    </div>\n    <div class=\"col\">\n      <div class=\"p-3\">Row column</div>\n    </div>\n  </div>\n</div>","language":"html"},{"id":"no-gutters","type":"heading","en":"No gutters","level":2},{"id":"no-gutters--paragraph-1","type":"paragraph","en":"The gutters between columns in our predefined grid classes can be removed with <code>.g-0</code>. This removes the negative <code>margin</code>s from <code>.row</code> and the horizontal <code>padding</code> from all immediate children columns."},{"id":"no-gutters--paragraph-2","type":"paragraph","en":"<strong>Need an edge-to-edge design?</strong> Drop the parent <code>.container</code> or <code>.container-fluid</code> and add <code>.mx-0</code> to the <code>.row</code> to prevent overflow."},{"id":"no-gutters--paragraph-3","type":"paragraph","en":"In practice, here’s how it looks. Note that you can continue to use this with all other predefined grid classes (including column widths, responsive tiers, reorders, and more)."},{"id":"no-gutters--example-1","type":"demo","key":"6d9efad30723746c932e","height":147},{"id":"no-gutters--code-1","type":"code","value":"<div class=\"row g-0 text-center\">\n  <div class=\"col-sm-6 col-md-8\">.col-sm-6 .col-md-8</div>\n  <div class=\"col-6 col-md-4\">.col-6 .col-md-4</div>\n</div>","language":"html"},{"id":"change-the-gutters","type":"heading","en":"Change the gutters","level":2},{"id":"change-the-gutters--paragraph-1","type":"paragraph","en":"Classes are built from the <code>$gutters</code> Sass map which is inherited from the <code>$spacers</code> Sass map."},{"id":"change-the-gutters--code-1","type":"code","value":"$grid-gutter-width: 1.5rem;\n$gutters: (\n  0: 0,\n  1: $spacer * .25,\n  2: $spacer * .5,\n  3: $spacer,\n  4: $spacer * 1.5,\n  5: $spacer * 3,\n);","language":"scss"}],"demos":[{"key":"6c692653c0e7ca7651d3","html":" <div class=\"container px-4 text-center\">\n  <div class=\"row gx-5\">\n    <div class=\"col\">\n      <div class=\"p-3\">Custom column padding</div>\n    </div>\n    <div class=\"col\">\n      <div class=\"p-3\">Custom column padding</div>\n    </div>\n  </div>\n</div> ","attrs":{"class":"bd-example m-0 border-0 bd-example-cols"},"sprite":""},{"key":"afc57d66e51f611fa6d3","html":" <div class=\"container overflow-hidden text-center\">\n  <div class=\"row gx-5\">\n    <div class=\"col\">\n      <div class=\"p-3\">Custom column padding</div>\n    </div>\n    <div class=\"col\">\n      <div class=\"p-3\">Custom column padding</div>\n    </div>\n  </div>\n</div> ","attrs":{"class":"bd-example m-0 border-0 bd-example-cols"},"sprite":""},{"key":"a316e9a220e5a690cc86","html":" <div class=\"container overflow-hidden text-center\">\n  <div class=\"row gy-5\">\n    <div class=\"col-6\">\n      <div class=\"p-3\">Custom column padding</div>\n    </div>\n    <div class=\"col-6\">\n      <div class=\"p-3\">Custom column padding</div>\n    </div>\n    <div class=\"col-6\">\n      <div class=\"p-3\">Custom column padding</div>\n    </div>\n    <div class=\"col-6\">\n      <div class=\"p-3\">Custom column padding</div>\n    </div>\n  </div>\n</div> ","attrs":{"class":"bd-example m-0 border-0 bd-example-cols"},"sprite":""},{"key":"76dd58cc38bef2794b66","html":" <div class=\"container text-center\">\n  <div class=\"row g-2\">\n    <div class=\"col-6\">\n      <div class=\"p-3\">Custom column padding</div>\n    </div>\n    <div class=\"col-6\">\n      <div class=\"p-3\">Custom column padding</div>\n    </div>\n    <div class=\"col-6\">\n      <div class=\"p-3\">Custom column padding</div>\